    "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
    "headline": "Beach Hazards Statement issued October 20 at 1:29PM PDT until October 20 at 11:00PM PDT by NWS San Diego CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...Dangerous rip currents and breaking waves. Surf of 3 to\n5 feet with local sets to 6 feet. Highest surf on south and\nsouthwest facing beaches.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County coastal areas and Orange County\ncoastal areas.\n\n* WHEN...Through this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Areas of hazardous swimming conditions. Rip currents\ncan pull swimmers and surfers out to sea. Waves can wash\npeople off beaches and rocks, and capsize small boats near\nshore.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Minor beach erosion may occur across\nsouth- facing beaches.",
    "instruction": "Remain out of the water to avoid hazardous swimming conditions.",
